/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342657/field-3/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" :answer/id #uuid "de965145-bccc-5a63-8258-67af5011c9dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342657/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d826c523-6086-521d-b16f-8a36039323c9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342657/field-3/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer-field/choices ["q-342657/field-3/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" "q-342657/field-3/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342657/field-4/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer/id #uuid "770a8cba-ea2f-530b-ad39-7d2428fa85f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342657/field-4/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" :answer/id #uuid "0659e5fb-ad00-5ec2-8b69-093893de172d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342657/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "765a71d0-a1bf-52b5-a629-ea0c8eaea08c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342657/field-4/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer-field/choices ["q-342657/field-4/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" "q-342657/field-4/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342657" :question/id #uuid "24b6f004-4c8b-5565-a4ef-1d172930ca34" :question/math-academy-id "q-342657" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+2, & x\\in [-2,0] \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}, & x\\in (0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ because $\\frac{1}{x}\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/8e5eec10427a7061a05c0bd1228ce1146234bf2b09d75bb86ba83b28fbe178d9.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ because ${F}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}(x+2)=-2+2=0\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{1}{x}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and II are false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/4afcdf86f777b9c7afc8af31b36cde4b80cfe394fd908db1ccd47ef48dff1617.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342657/field-1" "q-342657/field-2" "q-342657/field-3" "q-342657/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342657"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-1/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" :answer/id #uuid "e6c307bb-bf83-52c3-9960-d9b58e1f1ec9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-1/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer/id #uuid "d7c7c192-0d6b-5503-9773-80ca89f0c61d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5170f572-530f-58cb-93cb-a29c0a55f27c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342949/field-1/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer-field/choices ["q-342949/field-1/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" "q-342949/field-1/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-2/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer/id #uuid "d6039bbd-1613-5c11-b3bf-ddcb514c89ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-2/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" :answer/id #uuid "89945b8d-8fe3-545f-9df4-6439452b0856" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b34575d-d00a-5bf3-aa7d-5689b0b2150f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342949/field-2/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer-field/choices ["q-342949/field-2/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" "q-342949/field-2/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-3/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" :answer/id #uuid "a5950238-24a9-5cb9-9c0b-da67fbee88ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-3/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer/id #uuid "4062c862-3e4f-5e7b-8a91-de3e98dc5f33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e821172c-774f-5553-8b7d-99e66f9662ba" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342949/field-3/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer-field/choices ["q-342949/field-3/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" "q-342949/field-3/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-4/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer/id #uuid "eb6a5eac-a965-59f1-a085-89c92b83abbf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-4/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d" :answer/id #uuid "2a434b50-ba90-587d-aa80-8828ecab766d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "bee8795e-5501-5d7c-8069-49b1ebd243b5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342949/field-4/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" :answer-field/choices ["q-342949/field-4/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea2652" "q-342949/field-4/b078929a2c7936cc58936f9a3dc3ad9d34bf096fcbea293ffdde0acd0defc39d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342949" :question/id #uuid "b9c0da7f-f06a-5e11-82dc-9399c7844b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-342949" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x+1, & x\\in [-3,0] \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\in (0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ because $\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/7736417b068541a1609efa46e9824cd3f65cd34856c1d2f5d0ec7258ec883b5c.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ because ${F}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}(2x+1)=2(-3)+1=-5\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and II are false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/ac4d89fcccca99bebaeab4b44baac9c5c03651c38cef7e4d14cfe57978d066b7.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342949/field-1" "q-342949/field-2" "q-342949/field-3" "q-342949/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/valida