y "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343247/field-3/72c0bdb6bf3a2ef2c22611c3bd02136ae378bd0b4861ce9c9e72d9638dabbd4d" :answer-field/choices ["q-343247/field-3/b7c4afe2886f3796e8666f84755396b17f71ab5bf09a1d50cad6b937e9248dc0" "q-343247/field-3/007a22c8ca06969344d1d2e887ec366d871a66f338ddaf2e8228174911077972" "q-343247/field-3/72c0bdb6bf3a2ef2c22611c3bd02136ae378bd0b4861ce9c9e72d9638dabbd4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-4/bc9d94f2314f463873074f976c5ed4b12703edb691e7cb0a7fadede6c04f15aa" :answer/id #uuid "131b640d-b3f4-5975-aed9-fc601fe01ee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-4/597c53c6932788fb25691ac58249bc7ce8ae20b320bedae61c51eda57272d6ab" :answer/id #uuid "fd7529cd-37f0-5e90-80e0-f5cdbb2afacc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{75(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-4/02a726d4a37ef459f4a44518f52805207d07127368d28689a239fb7cfda56438" :answer/id #uuid "3ffb9dcf-aaaf-5a11-bfcd-d12bb5487949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-4/f768a6a976dce349ab06e0b3a28a5dd7ecd509d6f26c678a3db6694095bc761d" :answer/id #uuid "0af2ac91-651e-5dc6-9c91-cd2ec7a482ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7557fe4-ab09-56b2-85d8-21a8958a39f9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343247/field-4/f768a6a976dce349ab06e0b3a28a5dd7ecd509d6f26c678a3db6694095bc761d" :answer-field/choices ["q-343247/field-4/bc9d94f2314f463873074f976c5ed4b12703edb691e7cb0a7fadede6c04f15aa" "q-343247/field-4/597c53c6932788fb25691ac58249bc7ce8ae20b320bedae61c51eda57272d6ab" "q-343247/field-4/02a726d4a37ef459f4a44518f52805207d07127368d28689a239fb7cfda56438" "q-343247/field-4/f768a6a976dce349ab06e0b3a28a5dd7ecd509d6f26c678a3db6694095bc761d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-5/15ac0f5aa15d807d2f3d0f3f9a0a2407a5be08159fc4056c6a1c213ca1e53a5a" :answer/id #uuid "69393008-162b-5dd7-8b7c-a7760a9d0a2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-5/ade30588369467ed17c4af61ad49608bfa1a3009c7f9e8c9242bd289cac31ad6" :answer/id #uuid "64efde4c-3bc0-5f59-a8be-ccc48d6d9c10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247/field-5" :answer-field/id #uuid "a04cbf9a-d9d8-5bb8-8c52-1c5722c4e578" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343247/field-5/ade30588369467ed17c4af61ad49608bfa1a3009c7f9e8c9242bd289cac31ad6" :answer-field/choices ["q-343247/field-5/15ac0f5aa15d807d2f3d0f3f9a0a2407a5be08159fc4056c6a1c213ca1e53a5a" "q-343247/field-5/ade30588369467ed17c4af61ad49608bfa1a3009c7f9e8c9242bd289cac31ad6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343247" :question/id #uuid "7379723f-56d8-5cec-a825-183cb7d85e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-343247" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $10$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5$ defined on $[-5,5).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $10$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5∼-\\frac{5}{4}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-\\frac{5}{4}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-5,5),$\n\n- continuous on $[-5,5),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-5)=F(5),$ if we extend the value at $x=5$ using the formula $F(x)=-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5.$\n\nTherefore, the $10$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{5}{4})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-15(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343247/field-1" "q-343247/field-2" "q-343247/field-3" "q-343247/field-4" "q-343247/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34