 "q-342963/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "027e74fe-079f-57f8-a248-5ec3aa1f9e7c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342963/field-4/f831061a2f44778f81227309eb96b4800816328f7a8b21b5f7d53636798c6fd1" :answer-field/choices ["q-342963/field-4/f831061a2f44778f81227309eb96b4800816328f7a8b21b5f7d53636798c6fd1" "q-342963/field-4/529fdbbabed630674bdd9333925f335a53f6ab44c4ef17ce2a7e485e481122bb" "q-342963/field-4/3be13c4430d58b350844582f8449326988c5fb592e67a6de397724cca69a72e8" "q-342963/field-4/11cfb29babb028c1112f437fd43476ec03e2b8dfff00a77eaeff7144a4fbe8e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342963/field-5/4f1cc41f8ce9a3ee526cae63a3c1c702a1e792404302f4907ff1b52447a8e94f" :answer/id #uuid "2ee5ac9d-41e7-556a-9a28-a4e771600c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342963/field-5/02ed36065101387bcf15b45d2220bec17bd5ee8469eadf19e4c6f098cb65b0a2" :answer/id #uuid "8de7aaf4-3a9a-51c2-aff3-1b09494d2d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342963/field-5" :answer-field/id #uuid "44f0ec22-25c5-56d9-b424-29c327d765c7" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342963/field-5/02ed36065101387bcf15b45d2220bec17bd5ee8469eadf19e4c6f098cb65b0a2" :answer-field/choices ["q-342963/field-5/4f1cc41f8ce9a3ee526cae63a3c1c702a1e792404302f4907ff1b52447a8e94f" "q-342963/field-5/02ed36065101387bcf15b45d2220bec17bd5ee8469eadf19e4c6f098cb65b0a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342963" :question/id #uuid "624aeef7-3c3e-595d-97ee-b38fb454f235" :question/math-academy-id "q-342963" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-3{x}^{2}+1$ defined on $[-3,3).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-6x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-3{x}^{2}+1∼-8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-6x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-3,3),$\n\n- continuous on $[-3,3),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-3)=F(3),$ if we extend the value at $x=3$ using the formula $F(x)=-3{x}^{2}+1.$\n\nTherefore, the $6$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{x}^{2}+1) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-8)+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -6x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -6x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-36(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\ -6x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{36(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342963/field-1" "q-342963/field-2" "q-342963/field-3" "q-342963/field-4" "q-342963/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342963"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343380/field-2/b7c4afe2886f3796e8666f84755396b17f71ab5bf09a1d50cad6b937e9248dc0" :answer/id #uuid "159576c2-a6eb-59b0-ac55-b7c67187618f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "periodic" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343380/field-2/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0" :answer/id #uuid "dce6e597-e3f8-5d4a-8ce8-e79f692769de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343380/field-2/f021ba97381fbd3dfd1e299d63f0ee5efd946e117c64a06daa1715e288d9d01c" :answer/id #uuid "0661e56c-183e-5dfe-8a8b-5098fb468d0a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343380/field-2/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" :answer/id #uuid "22f47ab5-f508-553a-b48a-79de00e4103c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343380/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e5e5c12-6932-5a70-9f11-1721a658ebb4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343380/field-2/f021ba97381fbd3dfd1e299d63f0ee5efd946e117c64a06daa1715e288d9d01c" :answer-field/choices ["q-343380/field-2/b7c4afe2886f3796e8666f84755396b17f71ab5bf09a1d50cad6b937e9248dc0" "q-343380/field-2/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0" "q-343380/field-2/f021ba97381fbd3dfd1e299d63f0ee5efd946e117c64a06daa1715e288d9d01c" "q-343380/field-2/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343380/field-3/a4b3b5b610d8ad8f63c3d1ed5cd8c488