$f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}∼-2x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-2,2).$ \nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2}))\\text{d}t \\\\ {[-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{x} & ∼[-2t]_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{2}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3} & ∼-2x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{48(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343380/field-2" "q-343380/field-3" "q-343380/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-343341/field-1/23f2a7a35d5ad4412a57fe8263a4a0d9bc04d4ac82fe436f10b2386230dc3e85" :answer/id #uuid "fcbb6c50-b160-5922-b322-84e19db83ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{10})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343341/field-1/ade30588369467ed17c4af61ad49608bfa1a3009c7f9e8c9242bd289cac31ad6" :answer/id #uuid "7